\paragraph{RDM construction.}
For each task, we pair all time steps from 50 demonstrations within that task ($N$ observations per task).
We compute the $N \times N$ representational dissimilarity matrix (RDM) for each representation source using pairwise Euclidean distances across the full trajectory.
An analogous RDM is computed for the 7-dimensional action vectors using Euclidean distance.

\paragraph{RSA statistic.}
We measure the alignment between a representation RDM and the action RDM via Spearman rank correlation $\rho$ over the upper-triangular entries of each matrix.
Higher $\rho$ indicates that observations that are nearby in representation space also tend to require similar actions.

\paragraph{Task-level analysis.}
We compute RSA separately for each of the 10 LIBERO-Goal tasks using within-task observation pairs, then report the mean $\rho$ across tasks.
This within-task procedure ensures that RSA reflects how well representations capture the action structure \emph{within} a task, avoiding conflation with between-task variation.

